        "contact": {
          "url": "https://baconipsum.com/json-api/"
        },
        "description": "The Bacon Ipsum JSON API is a REST interface for generating meaty lorem ipsum text that can be utilized by any application. Users can specify parameters such as type of text, number of paragraphs, and format to get tailored responses.",
        "servers": [
          {
            "description": "Production server",
            "url": "https://baconipsum.com"
          }
        ],
        "title": "Bacon Ipsum API",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "tagline": "Generate meat-themed lorem ipsum filler text as JSON, plain text, or HTML",
        "homepage": "https://baconipsum.com",
        "docs_url": "https://baconipsum.com/json-api/",
        "license_short": "No formal licence stated; free public API with no authentication",
        "license_md": "- No explicit licence terms are published on the Bacon Ipsum site or its API docs.\n- The service is publicly accessible without an API key or sign-up.\n- Attribution is not required, but linking back to [baconipsum.com](https://baconipsum.com) is a friendly courtesy.\n- Treat usage as best-effort; no SLA or rate-limit policy is documented.",
        "about_md": "[Bacon Ipsum](https://baconipsum.com) is a placeholder-text generator created by Pete Nelson that swaps the usual Latin lorem ipsum for a list of meaty words. The [JSON API](https://baconipsum.com/json-api/) wraps the same generator behind a single REST endpoint so any application can request filler copy on demand.\n\nWhat you get from the API:\n\n- A single `GET https://baconipsum.com/api/` endpoint that returns generated paragraphs.\n- A `type` parameter (`all-meat` or `meat-and-filler`) to control the word mix.\n- A `paras` parameter for paragraph count, or `sentences` to request a specific sentence count instead.\n- A `start-with-lorem=1` flag to begin output with the classic \"Bacon ipsum dolor sit amet\" opener.\n- A `format` parameter (`json`, `text`, or `html`) and a `callback` parameter for JSONP.\n\nThe API is publicly reachable without authentication and CORS is enabled, so it can be called directly from browser code. No rate limits or licence terms are published; the underlying generator is also distributed as the open-source [Any Ipsum](https://github.com/petenelson/wp-any-ipsum) WordPress plugin.",
        "entity_desc": {
          "text_generation": "Generated meat-themed placeholder text returned as a JSON array of paragraphs (or plain text / HTML) from `GET /api/` with parameters like `type`, `paras`, `sentences`, `start-with-lorem`, and `format`."
        },
